      "key": {
        "uuid": "21d59f21_1c83343b",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/INetdEventCallback.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000451
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-18T10:07:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In order to avoid race conditions, I think we need to include the String hostname, which may be empty.\n\nFor logging purposes I think we should include the IP address of the nameserver that validated.  This won\u0027t be put into LinkProperties but we can debug-log it for good measure. Lorenzo suggests that we will probably want a boolean for validation status.  Initially we would only send up events when servers go from not validated to validated, but we might in future be able to detect SSL validation failures and bubble them up to ConnectivityService so that we can re-do captive portal detection.\n\nSo I proposed:\n\n    ...(int netId, String nameserver, String hostname, boolean isValidated)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "707e79f32b47429e6d60899fd8bb3c1fe749dc69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8bbe5ad_40b37a97",
